{
  "where_we_lag": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Etelä-Karjala's crude curative treatment share is 18.9% (95% CI 15.1–23.3; n=67/355) versus 27.0% (4009/14873) nationally, with its 95% confidence interval excluding the national value.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:curative:Etelä_Karjalan_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:curative"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Across overlapping treatment categories, Etelä-Karjala's crude shares are 18.9% (95% CI 15.1–23.3; n=67/355) versus 27.0% (4009/14873) nationally for curative, 21.4% (95% CI 17.5–26.0; n=76/355) versus 30.4% (4522/14873) for life-prolonging, and 31.3% (95% CI 26.7–36.3; n=111/355) versus 39.5% (5871/14873) for symptomatic treatment; each 95% confidence interval excludes the national value.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:curative:Etelä_Karjalan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:curative",
          "cty:life_prolonging:Etelä_Karjalan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:life_prolonging",
          "cty:symptomatic:Etelä_Karjalan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:symptomatic"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In Kuva 16, which provides the report's only county-level age-adjusted shares (digitised at ±0.5 percentage points precision), the curative gap holds for men at 18.9% (95% CI 13.5–25.7) versus 26.7% nationally (95% confidence interval excludes the national value), while for women at 19.8% (95% CI 13.4–29.0) versus 26.9% nationally, the 95% confidence interval includes the national value.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "fig:age_adjusted_only_kuva16",
          "k16:curative:men:Etelä_Karjalan_hyvinvointialue",
          "k16:curative:men:national",
          "k16:curative:women:Etelä_Karjalan_hyvinvointialue",
          "k16:curative:women:national"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Across overlapping treatment categories, Etelä-Karjala's crude share with no treatment record within 12 months is 42.8% (95% CI 37.8–48.0; n=152/355), with a 95% confidence interval excluding and above the national 27.5% (4089/14873), and its crude recorded multidisciplinary team (MDT) meeting share is 0.0% (95% CI 0.0–1.1; n=0/355), with a 95% confidence interval excluding and below the national 6.0% (893/14873).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Etelä_Karjalan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Etelä_Karjalan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "how_sure_are_we": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Public data cannot separate care gaps from recording gaps in Etelä-Karjala's crude treatment shares, cannot adjust for stage or most age differences, and omit key pathway timestamps.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:no_treatment_record:Etelä_Karjalan_hyvinvointialue",
        "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
        "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
        "fig:age_adjusted_only_kuva16",
        "bs:coverage:Referral"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Because 'no treatment record within 12 months' mixes untreated patients and unrecorded care across overlapping treatment categories, Etelä-Karjala's crude 42.8% share (95% CI 37.8–48.0; n=152/355) above the national 27.5% (4089/14873) means low crude treatment shares may partly reflect unrecorded treatment, while its crude 0.0% (95% CI 0.0–1.1; n=0/355) MDT share versus 6.0% (893/14873) measures HILMO recording from direct contacts, not care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Etelä_Karjalan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Etelä_Karjalan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:39e6ba43a9"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Taulukko 11 county shares are crude with separate limitations: they are not age-adjusted (age-adjusted county shares appear only in Kuva 16), and separately they cannot be stage-adjusted because stage at diagnosis is missing for about 48% of patients; moreover, a journal article finding about 90% HILMO concordance with the Cancer Registry concerns diagnosis only, not treatment recording.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "fig:age_adjusted_only_kuva16",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f",
          "lit:hilmo_90"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Public data omit symptom onset, referral dates, specialist visit or treatment start dates (showing only a 93.6% 12-month HILMO visit share), and imaging waits (showing only that about 20% of diagnoses rest on clinical findings like imaging alone), while primary care visits are not included in the report's data and occupational health is not mentioned.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:First_specialist_visit",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
          "bs:coverage:Imaging",
          "q:5eb155decc",
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "q:323de0d90d"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Preliminary, unpublished national study figures reported by Yle MOT indicate that lung cancer takes 155 days on average from initial symptoms to treatment in Finland—compared with 107 days in Sweden and 67 days in Denmark—consisting of 56 days of patient delay, 41 days in primary care, and 58 days in specialist care, though county-level delays are unknown.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "mot:total_fi",
          "mot:total_se",
          "mot:total_dk",
          "mot:patient",
          "mot:primary",
          "mot:specialist"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "what_to_do_first": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "The team recommends auditing stage, drug treatment, and MDT recording completeness, tracking access times using THL 21/2016 definitions with handover alerts, and standardising referrals and diagnostic coordination.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "rec:3",
        "rec:1",
        "rec:2",
        "q:950a2f797b",
        "thl:21_2016",
        "q:556431a0c2"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Given Etelä-Karjala's crude 42.8% (95% CI 37.8–48.0; n=152/355) versus 27.5% (4089/14873) no-treatment-record and 0.0% (95% CI 0.0–1.1; n=0/355) versus 6.0% (893/14873) MDT shares across overlapping treatment categories, plus 48% missing stage, the team recommends publishing county recording completeness for stage, drug treatment, and MDT coding while the STM roadmap (measure 3.2.1) plans a quality registry (decree update by 2026–2028; 90% coverage indicator).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:3",
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Etelä_Karjalan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Etelä_Karjalan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:950a2f797b",
          "q:f07a34a300",
          "q:4a856bd695"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Because the Health Care Act (§52) sets no legal maximum time for a cancer suspicion and national pathway monitoring is lacking, the team recommends reporting access times using THL guidance Ohjaus 21/2016 definitions for 16 cancers with handover alerts, while the STM roadmap (measure 3.1.2) plans national cancer-specific pathway descriptions and access times for five cancers by 2026–2028.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:1",
          "law:no_max",
          "q:4e702a20fe",
          "thl:21_2016",
          "q:24169121a4",
          "q:ed87906241",
          "q:def306014c"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Since referrals follow local instructions and a mentor insight notes that a weak referral receives a lower urgency rating in specialist care, the team recommends adopting a KYS-style referral template, a rule to refer persistent symptoms after a normal X-ray (found only in KYS's regional pathway document), and a diagnostic-phase contact person (absent from reviewed regional pathway documents).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "q:556431a0c2",
          "mentor:kaisa_referral",
          "reg:kys_template",
          "reg:kys_persistent",
          "reg:only_kys_xray",
          "reg:named_contact"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The team's recommended referral and coordination steps anticipate national plans: the Filha National Lung Cancer Programme's diagnostics recommendation (with primary-care referral criteria and recommended time limits) is to be carried out before the 2030 mid-term evaluation, while the STM roadmap plans standardised referral criteria for at least the five most common cancers (measure 2.5.2) and care-coordinator guidance (measure 1.2.3) by 2026–2028.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "q:29b792498e",
          "q:8f358a9de6",
          "q:614febebf2",
          "q:9a1cd194f5",
          "q:c61439b30f",
          "q:fc81032a80",
          "q:abcbb06ae3"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
